{
  "schema": "museum-cna-internal-type-classification/1",
  "categories": {
    "constraint-concept": "A template whose parameter is constrained by an internal concept. Callers pass ordinary public element types (Color, float, byte, Vector4...) and never name the concept, so the member is ordinary public API and stays in the demonstration denominator.",
    "defaulted-internal-parameter": "A public constructor whose trailing parameter has an internal type with a default value. Callers that rely on the default never name the internal type; only the defaulted parameter is upstream leakage.",
    "public-alias-or-proxy": "A public alias or a returned proxy implemented in a detail namespace. Applications use it through the public name (or the proxy's implicit conversion) without naming the detail type, so it counts as ordinary public API.",
    "renderer-plumbing": "A backend hook (renderer objects, GPU draw parameters, renderer-thread leases) that is public or protected only so CNA's own renderers and effects can reach it. It is not application API: the museum must not call it, it is not demonstrated, and it is not counted as missing museum coverage. Upstream fix: make it private with friend access or move it behind an internal accessor.",
    "pipeline-internal-type": "Public content-pipeline API whose signature returns, takes or exposes an internal XNB codec type. An application can only use the result by touching CNA::Internal::Xnb fields, so every use is upstream leakage. Upstream fix: a public result/options type (for ContentCompiler::Compile, e.g. a public CompiledXnb { bytes, rootReaderName }) or a public alias in the pipeline namespace."
  },
